    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "PHASE 4 \u2014 DYNAMIC TYPE RESOLUTION (why this exists)\n\nThe problem this replaces:\nOld design needed one hardcoded branch per document type \u2014\nAI Agent + Parser + Formatter \u00d7 60+ types = 150+ duplicate nodes.\nUnmaintainable, and adding a new type meant copy-pasting a whole branch.\n\nThe fix \u2014 one generic pipeline, driven by a Data Table:\n\nExtract docType:\n  Reads docRoles (set by Extract & Prepare's filename detection)\n  Picks the PRIMARY document's role \u2192 e.g. \"SMPC\", \"PHYS_CHEM\"\n\nGet type config:\n  Looks up that docType in the \"GPMI Review Type Config\" Data Table\n  Returns that type's own splitCode / systemMessage / parserMergeCode /\n  formatReportCode / formatHtmlCode \u2014 stored as plain text, not nodes\n\nMerge Config:\n  n8n quirk: the Data Table node's own output REPLACES the incoming\n  item \u2014 it doesn't merge with what was already flowing (userMessage,\n  docRoles). This node stitches the config row back onto the real\n  document data so both are available together for everything downstream.\n\nSplit (generic):\n  Executes that type's OWN splitCode dynamically (via new Function()) \u2014\n  e.g. a type-specific section-splitting script, or nothing at all for\n  types that review the whole document in one pass (empty splitCode =\n  passthrough, no code change needed).\n\nNet effect: adding document type #61 means adding ONE row to the Data\nTable \u2014 pasting in that type's real code \u2014 never touching this pipeline.",
