    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "PHASE 4C \u2014 DYNAMIC FORMATTING (one engine, per-type code)\n\nOnce the loop finishes, every AI response for this run is parsed and\nformatted using that SAME type's own stored code \u2014 executed\ndynamically, not hardcoded per type:\n\nParse & Merge (generic):\n  Runs the type's own parserMergeCode \u2014 merges/validates the AI's JSON\n\nRecombine After Parse:\n  Same recombine pattern again: that type's own parsing logic builds a\n  clean report object from scratch, which drops formatReportCode /\n  formatHtmlCode along the way. This step re-attaches them from Merge\n  Config before the next two steps need them.\n\nFormat Report (generic) \u2192 Format HTML (generic):\n  Run that type's own formatReportCode, then formatHtmlCode \u2014 producing\n  the plain-text report and the final HTML report exactly as that\n  type's original, hand-written formatter would have.\n\nWhy this matters at 60+ files: none of these 4 nodes contain a single\nline of type-specific logic. They're the same 4 nodes for every type \u2014\nonly the CODE they execute (fetched from the Data Table) changes.",
